<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dornoch Firth</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dornoch Firth is a sea inlet on the east coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scottish-highlands">Scottish Highlands</a>, dividing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-ross">Easter Ross</a> to the south from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutherland">Sutherland</a> to the north. The cathedral town of Dornoch stands on its northern shore. Its estuary, sands and salt marshes are protected as a national scenic area and a nature reserve.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dornoch-firth.jpg" alt="Dornoch Firth" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sylvia duckworth · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shoreline_looking_across_Dornoch_Firth_-_geograph.org.uk_-_687442.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
